<Information title="Pandora’s Box" description="Gabriel Andrade's personal agent workspace and its Forge Gmail integration.">
  <p>Pandora’s Box is Gabriel Andrade’s personal workspace for agent-assisted engineering and operational automation. Forge supports his own job search: organizing opportunities, preparing reviewable application materials, and tracking application outcomes.</p>
  <h2>Why connect Gmail?</h2>
  <p>The Forge Gmail integration looks for replies related to tracked applications and recruiter conversations. It records status and notifies Gabriel, who handles the conversation. Gmail access is read-only: this integration does not send replies, create drafts, change labels, archive messages, or mark messages as read.</p>
  <h2>Personal use</h2>
  <p>This connection is operated by Gabriel for his own account. It is not a public email service, a mailing platform, or an invitation for other users to connect their accounts. Application delivery uses separately reviewed channels and permissions.</p>
  <p>Read the <a href="/pandora/privacy/">Gmail integration privacy notice</a> for the data accessed, stored, and processed, and the <a href="/pandora/terms/">terms of personal use</a>. The <a href="/work/pandora/">Pandora case study</a> describes the broader project.</p>
</Information>
